---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Source from '../components/Source.astro';
import {
  annualSeries,
  filingRecord,
  financialsSource,
  headline,
  itemOf,
  latestFiling,
  sectorSpending,
  sreDataset,
  verifiedFilings,
} from '../data/financials';

const peso = new Intl.NumberFormat('en-PH', {
  style: 'currency',
  currency: 'PHP',
  maximumFractionDigits: 0,
});
const pesoExact = new Intl.NumberFormat('en-PH', {
  style: 'currency',
  currency: 'PHP',
  minimumFractionDigits: 2,
});
const number = new Intl.NumberFormat('en-PH');

const latest = latestFiling;
const latestHeadline = latest ? headline(latest) : null;
const sectors = latest ? sectorSpending(latest) : [];
const sectorMax = Math.max(1, ...sectors.map((s) => s.value));
const sectorTotal = sectors.reduce((sum, s) => sum + s.value, 0);
const years = annualSeries();
const latestRecord = latest ? filingRecord(latest.filingId) : undefined;
const totalChecks = verifiedFilings.reduce((sum, f) => sum + f.reconciliation.total, 0);

/** Income composition of the latest filing, in the Total column. */
const incomeRows = latest
  ? [
      'local-sources',
      'tax-revenue',
      'real-property-tax',
      'tax-on-business',
      'other-taxes',
      'non-tax-revenue',
      'regulatory-fees',
      'service-user-charges',
      'economic-enterprises',
      'other-receipts',
      'external-sources',
      'national-tax-allotment',
      'other-national-shares',
      'inter-local-transfers',
      'extraordinary-receipts',
      'total-current-operating-income',
    ]
      .map((key) => itemOf(latest, key))
      .filter((item) => Boolean(item))
  : [];
---

<Base
  title="Finances"
  description="What the Municipality of Calatagan reported receiving and spending, quarter by quarter, with every figure traceable to the cell it came from in the original DILG filing."
>
  <h1>Municipal finances</h1>

  <p>
    Every quarter, the municipality files a <strong>Statement of Receipts and Expenditures</strong>
    with the Department of the Interior and Local Government. These are the figures from those
    filings.
  </p>

  {latest && latestHeadline && (
    <>
      <p class="lede">
        In the period to <strong>Q{latest.documentPeriod.quarter} CY{latest.documentPeriod.year}</strong>,
        Calatagan reported income of <strong>{peso.format(latestHeadline.income ?? 0)}</strong> and
        operating expenditure of <strong>{peso.format(latestHeadline.expenditures ?? 0)}</strong>.
        {latestHeadline.externalSources !== null && latestHeadline.income ? (
          <>
            {' '}Of that income,
            <strong>
              {' '}{Math.round(((latestHeadline.externalSources ?? 0) / latestHeadline.income) * 100)}%
            </strong>{' '}
            came from the national government rather than from local taxes and fees.
          </>
        ) : null}
      </p>

      <dl class="facts">
        <dt>Total income</dt>
        <dd>{pesoExact.format(latestHeadline.income ?? 0)}</dd>
        <dt>Locally raised</dt>
        <dd>{pesoExact.format(latestHeadline.localSources ?? 0)}</dd>
        <dt>National Tax Allotment</dt>
        <dd>{pesoExact.format(latestHeadline.nationalTaxAllotment ?? 0)}</dd>
        <dt>Operating expenditure</dt>
        <dd>{pesoExact.format(latestHeadline.expenditures ?? 0)}</dd>
        <dt>Cash balance, end</dt>
        <dd>{pesoExact.format(latestHeadline.cashBalanceEnd ?? 0)}</dd>
      </dl>

      <p class="src-note">
        Figures are cumulative within the calendar year: a Q{latest.documentPeriod.quarter} figure
        already includes the earlier quarters of CY{latest.documentPeriod.year}.
        {latestRecord && (
          <>
            {' '}<a href={latestRecord.downloadUrl} rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow">
              Download the original filing from DILG ↗
            </a>
          </>
        )}
      </p>
    </>
  )}

  <Source source={financialsSource} />

  <h2>Where the money comes from</h2>
  <p>
    Like most Philippine municipalities, Calatagan is funded mainly by its share of national taxes.
    The table shows the latest filing in full; every row names the cell it was read from.
  </p>
  <div class="scroll">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Line item</th>
          <th scope="col" class="num">General Fund</th>
          <th scope="col" class="num">SEF</th>
          <th scope="col" class="num">Total</th>
          <th scope="col">Cell</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {incomeRows.map((item) => (
          <tr class={`level-${item!.level}`}>
            <th scope="row">{item!.label}</th>
            <td class="num">{item!.generalFund ? number.format(item!.generalFund.value) : '—'}</td>
            <td class="num">{item!.sef ? number.format(item!.sef.value) : '—'}</td>
            <td class="num">{item!.total ? number.format(item!.total.value) : '—'}</td>
            <td><code>{item!.total?.cell ?? '—'}</code></td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="src-note">
    SEF is the Special Education Fund, a separate levy on real property that may only be spent on
    education. It is reported alongside the General Fund but is not interchangeable with it.
  </p>

  <h2>Where it goes</h2>
  <p>Operating expenditure by sector, for the same period.</p>
  <ul class="sectors">
    {sectors.map((sector) => (
      <li>
        <div class="sector-head">
          <span>{sector.label}</span>
          <span class="amount">
            {number.format(sector.value)}
            {sectorTotal > 0 && <span class="share"> · {Math.round((sector.value / sectorTotal) * 100)}%</span>}
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="bar" role="presentation">
          <span style={`width:${Math.max(0.5, (sector.value / sectorMax) * 100)}%`}></span>
        </div>
        <div class="cell-ref"><code>{sector.cell ?? '—'}</code></div>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  {years.length > 1 && (
    <>
      <h2>Full years</h2>
      <p>
        Fourth-quarter filings report the whole calendar year, so these rows are annual totals.
      </p>
      <div class="scroll">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Year</th>
              <th scope="col" class="num">Income</th>
              <th scope="col" class="num">Locally raised</th>
              <th scope="col" class="num">National Tax Allotment</th>
              <th scope="col" class="num">Operating expenditure</th>
              <th scope="col">Filing</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {years.map((row) => {
              const record = filingRecord(row.filing.filingId);
              return (
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row">CY{row.year}</th>
                  <td class="num">{number.format(row.income ?? 0)}</td>
                  <td class="num">{number.format(row.localSources ?? 0)}</td>
                  <td class="num">{number.format(row.nationalTaxAllotment ?? 0)}</td>
                  <td class="num">{number.format(row.expenditures ?? 0)}</td>
                  <td>
                    {record ? (
                      <a href={record.downloadUrl} rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow">DILG ↗</a>
                    ) : '—'}
                  </td>
                </tr>
              );
            })}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </>
  )}

  <h2>Every quarter on file</h2>
  <div class="scroll">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Period</th>
          <th scope="col" class="num">Income</th>
          <th scope="col" class="num">Operating expenditure</th>
          <th scope="col" class="num">Checks</th>
          <th scope="col">Original</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {verifiedFilings.map((filing) => {
          const figures = headline(filing);
          const record = filingRecord(filing.filingId);
          return (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Q{filing.documentPeriod.quarter} CY{filing.documentPeriod.year}</th>
              <td class="num">{number.format(figures.income ?? 0)}</td>
              <td class="num">{number.format(figures.expenditures ?? 0)}</td>
              <td class="num">{filing.reconciliation.passed}/{filing.reconciliation.total}</td>
              <td>
                {record ? (
                  <a href={record.downloadUrl} rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow">DILG ↗</a>
                ) : '—'}
              </td>
            </tr>
          );
        })}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>How these figures were checked</h2>
  <p>
    Each filing asserts a number of things about itself: that the General Fund and Special Education
    Fund columns add to the total column, that tax and non-tax revenue add to local sources, that
    the sectoral spending lines add to total expenditure, and so on. Every one of those identities
    is recomputed from the extracted values.
  </p>
  <p>
    Across <strong>{verifiedFilings.length}</strong> quarters,
    <strong> {number.format(totalChecks)}</strong> checks were recomputed and
    <strong> all passed</strong>. A filing whose own arithmetic did not hold would be excluded from
    this page rather than shown with a warning.
    {sreDataset.extractedCount > verifiedFilings.length && (
      <>
        {' '}{sreDataset.extractedCount - verifiedFilings.length} of{' '}
        {sreDataset.extractedCount} extracted filings are currently held back on that basis.
      </>
    )}
  </p>
  <p class="src-note">
    An SRE is not an audit. These are the municipality's own reported figures, filed with DILG. The
    Commission on Audit publishes separate audited statements which this project has not yet been
    able to obtain — see <a href="/sources">Sources</a>.
  </p>

  <style>
    .lede { font-size: 1.05rem; }
    .src-note { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.88rem; }
    tr.level-0 th, tr.level-0 td { font-weight: 700; }
    tr.level-1 th { font-weight: 600; }
    tr.level-3 th { padding-left: 26px; font-weight: 400; }
    tr.level-2 th { padding-left: 14px; font-weight: 500; }
    th[scope='row'] { text-align: left; }

    ul.sectors { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; }
    ul.sectors li { margin-bottom: 14px; }
    .sector-head {
      display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 12px;
      font-size: 0.9rem; margin-bottom: 4px; flex-wrap: wrap;
    }
    .amount { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; white-space: nowrap; }
    .share { color: var(--muted); }
    .bar { background: var(--line); border-radius: 3px; height: 8px; overflow: hidden; }
    .bar span { display: block; height: 100%; background: var(--accent); }
    .cell-ref { font-size: 0.72rem; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 2px; }
  </style>
</Base>
